WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.690
The idea behind
interactive Robogami

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:11.410
is that we want to make
robots easier to customize

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.700
and easier to create for people
who are not necessarily trained

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.350
in engineering design.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.890
And so we've basically
designed the system

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:25.750
which allows people to do
this design very intuitively.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.460
There are two main
ideas behind it.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.370
One is easy
fabrication, and one is

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.070
being able to virtually
verify that your robot will

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.110
work once it's been fabricated.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.090
On the fabrication
side, we've been

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.000
using 3D printing and
folding techniques in order

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.950
to make the
fabrication very easy.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.680
And on the functionality
side, we've

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.687
incorporated
simulations in order

00:00:46.687 --> 00:00:49.270
to make sure that the robot can
actually walk and can actually

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.830
perform tasks.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:53.520
3D printing has a
lot of advantages.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.340
You can print very
complex structures.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.740
They're very rigid.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.336
Whereas in 2D fabrication,
it's very fast

00:01:00.336 --> 00:01:02.710
and you can create basically
lightweight but still strong

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.310
structures.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.800
We took the advantage
of both of them

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.220
and we decided to 3D
print 2D patterns.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.240
So this allowed us to get
very rapid fabrication

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.810
of stiff structures that
are still lightweight.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.490
So designing a
robot is challenging

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.710
because there are many
aspects that must be designed.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:24.070
You have the 3D shape, the
motion, the electronics,

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:25.670
the control software.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.080
So how do you allow a casual
user of any skill level

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.470
to design all of these
aspects at the same time

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.350
to create a robot that
will solve the user's task?

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.500
Using our system, users
can create a robot body

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.150
by simply mixing and matching
parts from an existing catalog.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.970
And in the same way, the user
designs a motion for the robot

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.220
by selecting from a
list of suggestions

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.350
and modifying the
motion parameters.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.330
And all of the models
designed in the system

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:55.000
can be directly fabricated
and they are guaranteed

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.810
to work in the real world.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.530
So what makes interactive
Robogami powerful

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.720
is that it helps
users in designing

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.840
robots that will perform
tasks well by guiding

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.060
users in improving
both the motion

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.250
and the geometry of
the robot designs.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.030
For instance, making the
robots faster or more stable

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.250
or decreasing the
fabrication costs

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.670
to make them more affordable.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.390
What we've put into
the database are

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.990
a lot of wheeled robots
and some legged robots.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.730
You could combine
any part you want

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.390
in the database
with any other part

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.150
into as complex a
structure as you want.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.840
Our system would help you
make that design functional.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.430
What we envision
for the future is

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.340
that a user would be able
to go into the system

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.060
and basically define the
behavior of this robot in terms

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.260
of tasks.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.680
You can very quickly design
a tool that you can print out

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.140
and that will help you do
these tasks very cheaply, very

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:50.310
quickly, very easily.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.360
So the dream is
that this tool would

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.670
enable robots to
become prevalent

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.590
in our everyday lives.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.430
Since the system is geared
towards making design easy,

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.460
making fabrication
easy, then it's

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.450
basically lowering the barrier
to having everybody design

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.770
and create their own robots.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:13.120
[MUSIC PLAYING]

